      "rev_n_1_b737c7_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_b737c7_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_b737c7",
        "thought_text": "Store all dictionary words in a hash set for O(1) lookups. Iterate through each word, generate all possible strings by deleting exactly one character, and check if any generated string exists in the set. If yes, mark the original word as a typo.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794594424.8635051
      },
      "rev_n_2_5f6cca_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_5f6cca_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_5f6cca",
        "thought_text": "Since the total length of all strings is up to 1,000,000, an O(N * L) approach where N is the number of words and L is the average length is acceptable. We can optimize by only checking deletions for words that are longer than the shortest word in the dictionary, as a typo must be longer than the word it transforms into.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794594424.8635209
      },
      "rev_n_3_0ea1f8_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_0ea1f8_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_0ea1f8",
        "thought_text": "Sort the dictionary first to enable binary search or two-pointer techniques, though this adds O(N log N) overhead. Given the constraints and the simplicity of the deletion check, the hash set approach is likely faster and simpler to implement without risking TLE on edge cases.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794594424.8635297
      },
      "rev_n_4_57181e_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_57181e_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_57181e",
        "thought_text": "Store all words in a hash set for O(1) lookups. Iterate through each word, generate all strings by deleting exactly one character, and check if any result exists in the set. If yes, mark the original word as a typo.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-629798928938742626",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794594442.9880354
      },
      "rev_n_5_a43897_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_a43897_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_a43897",
        "thought_text": "Optimize by only checking words longer than 1 character (deleting from length 1 yields empty string, which isn't in the dictionary of non-empty words). Also, pre-filter words that are too short to possibly be typos based on the dictionary's minimum word length.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-629798928938742626",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794594442.9880514
      },
      "rev_n_6_f3fb10_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_f3fb10_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_f3fb10",
        "thought_text": "Sort the dictionary words by length first. For each word, only check against words in the set that are exactly one character shorter. This avoids generating strings and checking against longer words unnecessarily, though the hash set lookup remains the dominant factor.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-629798928938742626",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794594442.9880605
      },
      "rev_n_7_9f1b3e_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_9f1b3e_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_9f1b3e",
        "thought_text": "Store all dictionary words in a hash set for O(1) average-time lookups. Iterate through each word, generate all possible strings by deleting exactly one character, and check if the resulting string exists in the set. If it does, mark the original word as a typo.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4776997558927096980",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794594462.4908376
      },
      "rev_n_8_773d9c_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_773d9c_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_773d9c",
        "thought_text": "Optimize the brute force by first finding the minimum word length in the dictionary. Only process words longer than this minimum length, as a typo must be strictly longer than the valid word it transforms into. This reduces unnecessary checks for short words.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4776997558927096980",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794594462.4908535
      },
      "rev_n_9_cedd68_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_cedd68_0",
        "node_id": "n_9_cedd68",
        "thought_text": "Sort the dictionary words by length. For each word, only check deletions against words that are exactly one character shorter. This avoids checking against words of the same length or longer, leveraging the structural constraint that a typo reduces length by exactly one.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4776997558927096980",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
